sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: FootyLevels upload and media preparation
    accDescr: The client obtains a private upload capability, sends video directly to Supabase and finalizes through the API. A durable CPU job produces verified canonical playback and previews.
    autonumber
    participant App as iOS app
    participant API as Authenticated API
    participant DB as Firestore
    participant Store as Supabase private files
    participant CPU as CPU worker
    App->>API: Bootstrap profile and create project with Idempotency-Key
    API->>DB: Transactional owner-bound project creation
    DB-->>API: Existing or new project, state uploading
    API-->>App: Project ID and inputRevision
    App->>API: POST project upload-session: size, SHA-256, expectedRevision
    API->>DB: Reserve bounded source bytes and immutable upload record
    API->>Store: Mint signed upload capability
    API-->>App: Signed TUS capability and upload ID
    App->>Store: Direct resumable TUS upload of video-only source
    Store-->>App: Transfer progress and completion
    App->>API: POST upload finalize
    API->>Store: Stream and verify exact size and SHA-256
    API->>DB: Atomically commit source revision and prepareMedia job
    API-->>App: 202 Accepted, project preparing
    loop Bounded CPU polling every 120 seconds
        CPU->>DB: Transactionally claim eligible prepareMedia job
    end
    CPU->>Store: Download verified source to private staging
    CPU->>CPU: Credential-free FFprobe and FFmpeg validation and normalization
    CPU->>DB: Reserve all seven prepared outputs and verify live claim
    CPU->>Store: Upload canonical MP4 and six JPEG previews and verify stored hashes
    CPU->>DB: Fenced transaction: preparedMedia, state ready, job succeeded
    CPU->>CPU: Remove staging
    App->>API: Poll project until ready or rejected
    App->>API: POST project media-assets
    API-->>App: Owner-only five-minute allowlisted read map
    App->>Store: Download canonical playback and previews
